<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- Cultural actions (GAMEOPTION_CULTURE_ACTIONS; this game's own rules, docs/CULTURE.md).
     A city channels one action at a time from its cultural queue: iRate culture a turn is
     diverted for iDuration turns (scaled by the game speed's iTrainPercent), then the effect
     resolves on the target.

     Target:  OWN_OR_ALLY_CITY  a city of the caster's team or of a team it has a defensive pact with
              FOREIGN_CITY      a city of another team (or the barbarians) the caster has met
              ANY_CITY          either
     Hostile: NEVER, ALWAYS, or DIFFERENT_STATE_RELIGION (only when the target's owner has a
              state religion other than the one spread)
     Effect:  what completion does (the code's dispatch); its magnitudes are the CULTURE_*
              defines of RulesDefines.xml
     bScaledByEffect: the magnitude or chance is multiplied by the effectiveness E (never for a
              target of the caster's own team)
     bGarrisonResists: each land unit of the target's team on its plot adds
              CULTURE_GARRISON_RESIST to the defences M
     iThreatWeight: read by nothing yet (the future threat score)
     iMemoryWeight: points of cultural hostility (hostile) or friendship (friendly) the target's
              owner remembers when the action completes -->
